{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"enumerated","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s18EnumeratedSequenceV","text":"EnumeratedSequence","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/EnumeratedSequence"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Return Value","anchor":"return-value","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A sequence of pairs enumerating the sequence.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This example enumerates the characters of the string “Swift” and prints","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each character along with its place in the string.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["for (n, c) in \"Swift\".enumerated() {","    print(\"\\(n): '\\(c)'\")","}","\/\/ Prints \"0: 'S'\"","\/\/ Prints \"1: 'w'\"","\/\/ Prints \"2: 'i'\"","\/\/ Prints \"3: 'f'\"","\/\/ Prints \"4: 't'\""]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When you enumerate a collection, the integer part of each pair is a counter","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"for the enumeration, but is not necessarily the index of the paired value.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"These counters can be used as indices only in instances of zero-based,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"integer-indexed collections, such as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Array"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ContiguousArray"},{"text":". For","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other collections the counters may be out of range or of the wrong type","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to use as an index. To iterate over the elements of a collection with its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"indices, use the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"zip(_:_:)"},{"text":" function.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This example iterates over the indices and elements of a set, building a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"list consisting of indices of names with five or fewer letters.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let names: Set = [\"Sofia\", \"Camilla\", \"Martina\", \"Mateo\", \"Nicolás\"]","var shorterIndices: [Set<String>.Index] = []","for (i, name) in zip(names.indices, names) {","    if name.count <= 5 {","        shorterIndices.append(i)","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Now that the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"shorterIndices"},{"text":" array holds the indices of the shorter","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"names in the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"names"},{"text":" set, you can use those indices to access elements in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the set.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["for i in shorterIndices {","    print(names[i])","}","\/\/ Prints \"Sofia\"","\/\/ Prints \"Mateo\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"style":"note","name":"Complexity","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"O(1)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Returns a sequence of pairs (","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"x","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":"), where ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" represents a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"consecutive integer starting at zero and ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"x","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" represents an element of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the sequence.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"metadata":{"platforms":[{"introducedAt":"8.0","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"beta":false,"name":"iOS"},{"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"8.0","beta":false,"name":"iPadOS"},{"name":"Mac Catalyst","introducedAt":"13.0","beta":false,"unavailable":false,"deprecated":false},{"introducedAt":"10.10","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"beta":false,"name":"macOS"},{"unavailable":false,"name":"tvOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"9.0","beta":false},{"introducedAt":"1.0","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"beta":false,"name":"visionOS"},{"introducedAt":"2.0","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"beta":false,"name":"watchOS"}],"externalID":"s:STsE10enumerateds18EnumeratedSequenceVyxGyF::SYNTHESIZED::s:s18DiscontiguousSliceV","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"method","roleHeading":"Instance Method","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"enumerated"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"EnumeratedSequence","preciseIdentifier":"s:s18EnumeratedSequenceV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"title":"enumerated()","modules":[{"name":"Swift"}],"extendedModule":"Swift"},"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swift\/discontiguousslice\/enumerated()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/DiscontiguousSlice"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/DiscontiguousSlice\/enumerated()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/EnumeratedSequence":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/EnumeratedSequence","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swift\/enumeratedsequence","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EnumeratedSequence"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EnumeratedSequence"}],"title":"EnumeratedSequence","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An enumeration of the elements of a sequence or collection."}]},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift":{"role":"collection","abstract":[{"text":"Build apps using a powerful open language.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swift","title":"Swift","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/DiscontiguousSlice/enumerated()":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Returns a sequence of pairs (","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"x","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":"), where "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" represents a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"consecutive integer starting at zero and "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"x","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" represents an element of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the sequence."}],"role":"symbol","title":"enumerated()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"enumerated","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s18EnumeratedSequenceV","text":"EnumeratedSequence","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/DiscontiguousSlice\/enumerated()","url":"\/documentation\/swift\/discontiguousslice\/enumerated()"},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/DiscontiguousSlice":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A collection wrapper that provides access to the elements of a collection,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"indexed by a set of indices.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DiscontiguousSlice"}],"title":"DiscontiguousSlice","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DiscontiguousSlice","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swift\/discontiguousslice","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/DiscontiguousSlice"}}}